        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_977"/>
        <dc:title>Bulk ferromagnetism in the β-phase crystal of the p-nitrophenyl nitronyl nitroxide radical</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Transition to a ferromagnetic long-range ordered state was found at 0.60 K in the orthorhombic β-phase crystal of p-nitrophenyl nitronyl nitroxide (or 2-(4′-nitrophenyl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-4,5-dihydro-1H-imidazol-1-oxyl-3-N-oxide in the IUPAC nomenclature). This finding follows our recent discovery of the first organic bulk ferromagnet in the triclinic γ-phase crystal of the same compound.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>1991/11/15/</dc:date>
        <bib:pages>401-404</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
